                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Okay, previous review had a 14% approval rating because I gave it a thumbs up saying I needed more time with it. \n\nWell, here's everything - a link to a video where I discuss will be included in an edit tonight.\n\nHad a game breaking bug where I couldn't interact with any menus. I verified it was limited to just MIST VR before calling it quits.\n\nFor an interactive horror puzzler there are glaring flaws, here are a few:\n1) Limited/no sound other than ambient. No collision on objects etc (audio wise).\n2) If you touch an object to another object you drop it.\n3) Incredibly unfriendly interaction, to the point where I couldn't progress.\n4) Puzzle elements very basic and uninspired.\n5) Overpriced for the quality, I am fairly lenient on startups and even so this price point is inexcusable even if there are potentially some enjoyable moments to be found.\n\nCheck out my video for the full list. I do not advise buying this game.\n\nWill be putting in for a refund, I can tolerate a bad game - but I can't pay for a game that doesn't work as intended.",
